      "id": "lbarmfb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Heat is a form of energy that flows spontaneously from a region of higher temperature to a region of lower temperature.",
        "Temperature measures the degree of hotness or coldness of a body and determines the direction of heat flow.",
        "Heat transfer occurs through three distinct mechanisms: conduction in solids, convection in fluids, and radiation through vacuum.",
        "Thermal expansion occurs in solids, liquids, and gases upon heating, with gases exhibiting the maximum rate of expansion."
      ],
      "id": "34n1cp4"
    },
